    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d31">

                <pb facs="0068" n="48" xml:id="pg48"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">690B.9321/1–1653: Telegram</note>
                <head>No. 31<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Burma (Sebald) to the Department of
                            State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Rangoon</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1953-01-16T11:00:00+06:30">January 16, 1953—11
                        a.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1283. … KMT problem is beginning have
                    repercussions broader in scope than mere military dilemma. Foreign
                        Minister<anchor n="1" xml:id="d31-f1"/> also told me KMT problem is getting completely out of hand, intimated GUB seriously concerned. Hope Department will
                    speedily urge course of action all interested parties in endeavor assist GUB find practical solution.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sebald</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d31-f1" n="1" xml:id="d31-f1-content">
                <p>Sao Hkun Hkio.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
